From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alfred Ben <e0958604@u.nus.edu>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 17:24:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/5] explore, watcher: bound memory growth in long sessions

Long agent sessions grew the server without bound: the call graph build
held every file at once, every git HEAD change re-indexed the whole tree,
and call path results borrowed strings that were freed later.

- explore: build the call graph per file in its own arena, skip files
  with no function symbol, and copy only function bodies
- explore: drop the call graph when a file is removed
- explore: call path results own their strings
- watcher: on a git HEAD change, reconcile only the changed files
- watcher: drop files that turn binary or oversized, keep the trigram
  cap, and prune ignored directories
- mcp: fix a codedb_context deadlock on uncached top-site reads
